  "aiOverview": {
    "content": "Founded by Robert Redford in 1981, the Sundance Institute is a Park City-based nonprofit dedicated to discovering and supporting independent filmmakers, theater artists, and composers worldwide. It provides year-round artistic development through labs, grants, and mentorships, culminating in the renowned annual Sundance Film Festival. Sundance Institute Sundance Film Festival Core Programs and Initiatives Artist Support: The Institute operates labs and mentorship programs, including Feature Film, Documentary Documentary Film Program, and Theatre programs to support artists at every step of their creative journey, notes the Sundance Institute. Documentary Film Program Sundance Institute Sundance Film Festival: An annual, premier showcase for independent storytelling in Park City, Utah, that connects filmmakers with audiences. Indigenous Program: Dedicated to uplifting Indigenous voices, supporting Native storytellers, and decolonizing the screen. Women at Sundance: Focuses on fostering gender equality in the film industry through mentorship and support. Sundance Ignite: A program supporting artists aged 18 to 25 with labs, screenings, and creative mentorship, often featuring collaborations with Adobe. Adobe Producers Program: Provides year-round support to producers through labs, workshops, and grants. Support and Development Grants & Fellowships: The Institute offers numerous funding opportunities, such as the Documentary Fund and various artist grants. Documentary Fund Sundance Collab: An online community and learning platform. Impact: The institute helps launch the careers of independent artists and works to shift culture through new perspectives. Contact and Information Headquarters: Park City, Utah. Website: sundance.org sundance.org Support: Donations can be made to support the Institute's year-round artistic programs. support For the latest updates, you can follow the Institute on Instagram, watch content on YouTube, or connect with them on LinkedIn. Instagram YouTube LinkedIn",
